Date: Mon, 5 Oct 2026 11:26:32 +0000
Subject: [PATCH 1/2] MAP scrubber: timeline change marks + clock ticks (ticket
 draft 2026-10-05, Founder GO; not yet filed in Jira)

- Change mark where a formation_id's row state differs from its immediately preceding row;
  position = captured_at mapped linearly against the full history's earliest..latest.
- Color/shape by after-state (.fh-dot precedent, KRYL-1350): STRENGTHENING lime, WEAKENING blue,
  RECONFIGURATION purple diamond, all others Light Gray #e0e0dc. Same-timestamp changes combine
  into one mark (gray when after-states differ); native title hover lists each change with raw
  entity_a/entity_b, relationship_type, before -> after, captured_at.
- Clock ticks replace the edge-stagger ticks: hourly < 1 day, 12h for 1-7 days, daily beyond;
  overlapping labels skipped; zero range draws nothing.
- Verified headless Chromium, seeded histories (77-relationship case, mixed, zero range, >7 days,
  empty) at 900/1400/1570 px: no page errors, no label overlap, no horizontal overflow.
  Live-Dev real-query check still open.

